Major takeaways:

- The biggest AI opportunities may not be “AI features” at all, they’re rebuilding entire workflows and infrastructure around what becomes possible when intelligence is cheap… 

- Software is moving from being built exclusively for humans to being built for humans & agents. That changes everything from collaboration and interfaces to the underlying compute agents need to actually do work….

- The best AI companies are attacking problems where the old way was fundamentally constrained by human labor.. global compliance, coordination, software execution, etc.. 

- We’re still very early in figuring out what the company of the future looks like… smaller human teams, dramatically more leverage and potentially hundreds or thousands of agents operating alongside them… 

- AI isn’t just creating a new software category… it’s causing us to rethink the architecture of the company itself….

